commit.message:
feat(workspaces): the move engine, its journal and crash healing (NIW2-600)

Moves one finished item, with every file it owns (media, sidecar, thumbnail,
cursor track, edit project and assets, webcam track), from one workspace to
another, per ADR 0033:

- same volume: a hard link, then the source goes (no replace, no copy);
- another volume, or no hard links: a copy into the target's .kaipu/tmp,
  its sha256 compared, then placed; a mismatch leaves the source untouched;
- the target record reserves the stem first (Name (2) on a collision), so
  the media never lands before its sidecar;
- tags remap by slug, missing ones are created with the same name and color;
- a journal in userData is a hint only: healing inspects both disks and
  never deletes the only verified copy;
- refuses an unreadable record, a disconnected target, an untrusted target
  tag registry, an item dragged under 10 s ago, and a full drive.

